(581957, 60568, 6667, '<td valign="top">Well done.  I do have some distracting white specs showing up on my monitor''s version. . . and the materials weave becomes evident in the right foreground.  I do hope this makes it to the top three.  Enthralled by the green eyed  "look."  I would have liked to see the lower eyeliner a little more even. Is that a contact or was it enhanced? I won''t believe it if ou say it was her natural eye color. Despite all the comments, you still get high marks from me.  BOL</td>', 'Well done.  I do have some distracting white specs showing up on my monitor''s version. . . and the materials weave becomes evident in the right foreground.  I do hope this makes it to the top three.  Enthralled by the green eyed  "look."  I would have liked to see the lower eyeliner a little more even. Is that a contact or was it enhanced? I won''t believe it if ou say it was her natural eye color. Despite all the comments, you still get high marks from me.  BOL', '2004-02-16 14:19:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(581967, 60227, 6667, '<td valign="top">Who is the Willy Masconi?  Why not a combination shot rather than the jump ball?  This shot has a number of things going for it. . . and they are all very, very good. Simple, crisp and clear with enough depth of field to bring my attention to the eight ball immediately.  BOL  I do have a serious question.  What is the surface of the table?  It doesn''t look like the tradition felt.</td>', 'Who is the Willy Masconi?  Why not a combination shot rather than the jump ball?  This shot has a number of things going for it. . . and they are all very, very good. Simple, crisp and clear with enough depth of field to bring my attention to the eight ball immediately.  BOL  I do have a serious question.  What is the surface of the table?  It doesn''t look like the tradition felt.', '2004-02-16 14:28:35.000000', NULL, 1),
