(587086, 60688, 13728, '<td valign="top">I like this picture.  At first I interepreted the challenge in the exact same way, and then decided the  object should be black.  But after reading all of the forums on this before hand...I would have done a little spot editing here as long as you could have</td>', 'I like this picture.  At first I interepreted the challenge in the exact same way, and then decided the  object should be black.  But after reading all of the forums on this before hand...I would have done a little spot editing here as long as you could have', '2004-02-18 23:26:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(587092, 60511, 13728, '<td valign="top">Is it opposite day.  Looks very white to me.  But I do like the compsition</td>', 'Is it opposite day.  Looks very white to me.  But I do like the compsition', '2004-02-18 23:30:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(587180, 60200, 7969, '<td valign="top">Initially I rated this shot very low, I did not like this guy... on second look I asked myself why I did not like him, it''s cuz he is creepy...or at least the way the shot was processed made him look that way... he is like a nightmare image, and I find it disturbing to look at him, even as I comment, granted I can''t watch horror movies either, too sensitive, but in fairness to you, you have made me ''feel'' nothing good mind you but I think you deserve credit for producing such an emotive image....</td>', 'Initially I rated this shot very low, I did not like this guy... on second look I asked myself why I did not like him, it''s cuz he is creepy...or at least the way the shot was processed made him look that way... he is like a nightmare image, and I find it disturbing to look at him, even as I comment, granted I can''t watch horror movies either, too sensitive, but in fairness to you, you have made me ''feel'' nothing good mind you but I think you deserve credit for producing such an emotive image....', '2004-02-19 00:19:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(587384, 60159, 9906, '<td valign="top">This is an amazing shot that I''m sorry to say is probably getting too many comments of it''s too dark or no comments at all.  I love the minimalism of this while still being able to see the subject.  I won''t comment on the political statement of the title, but the shot does manage to give the feeling of the title!<br/>Very nice shot!  One of my favorites of the challenge!<br/>TC</td>', 'This is an amazing shot that I''m sorry to say is probably getting too many comments of it''s too dark or no comments at all.  I love the minimalism of this while still being able to see the subject.  I won''t comment on the political statement of the title, but the shot does manage to give the feeling of the title!Very nice shot!  One of my favorites of the challenge!TC', '2004-02-19 02:13:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(587385, 60394, 9906, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot.  A touch overexposed in a couple of spots but not obnoxiously so.  You managed to capture the detail nicely.  I would like to see this exposed one stop less just to see if the detail is still there!  At the very least a great study subject.<br/>TC</td>', 'Very nice shot.  A touch overexposed in a couple of spots but not obnoxiously so.  You managed to capture the detail nicely.  I would like to see this exposed one stop less just to see if the detail is still there!  At the very least a great study subject.TC', '2004-02-19 02:15:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(587388, 60655, 9906, '<td valign="top">Now this is dark.  I pride myself on having a monitor that is calibrated for dark shots but I can not make this out at all.  This makes me wonder how many comments you are getting about this issue....<br/>TC</td>', 'Now this is dark.  I pride myself on having a monitor that is calibrated for dark shots but I can not make this out at all.  This makes me wonder how many comments you are getting about this issue....TC', '2004-02-19 02:18:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(587389, 60492, 9906, '<td valign="top">First a question, is the pot actually black or are you working on the silhoette effect?  Now my comment.  Just the ever slightest amount of fill light to bring in just a smidge of detail at the top of the pot and this is spot on still life!<br/>TC</td>', 'First a question, is the pot actually black or are you working on the silhoette effect?  Now my comment.  Just the ever slightest amount of fill light to bring in just a smidge of detail at the top of the pot and this is spot on still life!TC', '2004-02-19 02:20:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(587390, 60475, 9906, '<td valign="top">A very difficult exposure and IMHO you missed it by just a touch.  Beautiful eyes and great composition, but you need just the ever slightest more detail in the fur (or less perhaps)<br/>TC</td>', 'A very difficult exposure and IMHO you missed it by just a touch.  Beautiful eyes and great composition, but you need just the ever slightest more detail in the fur (or less perhaps)TC', '2004-02-19 02:22:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(587394, 60645, 9906, '<td valign="top">I believe that this has gone past the point of photographic integrity and therefore I can not within the guidelines of the rule score it very highly...<br/>TC</td>', 'I believe that this has gone past the point of photographic integrity and therefore I can not within the guidelines of the rule score it very highly...TC', '2004-02-19 02:32:31.000000', NULL, 1),
