(591594, 60577, 6073, '<td valign="top">Daniel,<br/>Let me be one to say that I didn''t vote on your photo because I thought you colored the eyes in PS.   <br/> <br/>I have no clue if you did or not, but I didn''t vote you at 10 because I didn''t know.  Sorry.<br/> <br/>I would have gave you a 10, as this is an extraordinary photo.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Daniel,Let me be one to say that I didn''t vote on your photo because I thought you colored the eyes in PS.    I have no clue if you did or not, but I didn''t vote you at 10 because I didn''t know.  Sorry. I would have gave you a 10, as this is an extraordinary photo. ', '2004-02-21 00:16:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(591596, 60543, 4258, '<td valign="top">This is one of the most beautiful example of the kind of work I really enjoy "Implied Nudity" Fantastic!!<br/> <br/>However I did not vote on this image becuase for me it is not a picture with a black object as a subject.<br/> <br/>I would give this a 10 in almost any other challenge :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'This is one of the most beautiful example of the kind of work I really enjoy "Implied Nudity" Fantastic!! However I did not vote on this image becuase for me it is not a picture with a black object as a subject. I would give this a 10 in almost any other challenge :) ', '2004-02-21 00:25:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(591612, 60577, 4493, '<td valign="top">The eyes are this blue. I created a new layer in PS and desaturated it to b/w. I then erased the b/w eyes to show the blue eyes below. I did a light dodge on the whites of her eyes to bring those out more, but did not touch the blue color at all.<br/> <br/>-danny<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DJLuba:</b></div><hr/><i> Daniel,<br/>Let me be one to say that I didn''t vote on your photo because I thought you colored the eyes in PS.   <br/> <br/>I have no clue if you did or not, but I didn''t vote you at 10 because I didn''t know.  Sorry.<br/> <br/>I would have gave you a 10, as this is an extraordinary photo. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'The eyes are this blue. I created a new layer in PS and desaturated it to b/w. I then erased the b/w eyes to show the blue eyes below. I did a light dodge on the whites of her eyes to bring those out more, but did not touch the blue color at all. -danny Originally posted by DJLuba: Daniel,Let me be one to say that I didn''t vote on your photo because I thought you colored the eyes in PS.    I have no clue if you did or not, but I didn''t vote you at 10 because I didn''t know.  Sorry. I would have gave you a 10, as this is an extraordinary photo. ', '2004-02-21 00:37:33.000000', NULL, 0),
